1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,332
A failed transaction should not require a support ticket.

2
00:00:04,332 --> 00:00:12,034
GasBack lets a protocol sponsor a fixed rebate, paid only after the failure is independently verified.

3
00:00:12,334 --> 00:00:17,506
The sponsor authorizes this exact transaction intent before the user acts.

4
00:00:17,506 --> 00:00:23,147
The ticket fixes who gets paid, the amount, and the claim window.

5
00:00:23,147 --> 00:00:28,319
This is a fixed sponsor subsidy, not a full gas refund.

6
00:00:28,619 --> 00:00:31,682
Here is our actual Sepolia transaction.

7
00:00:31,682 --> 00:00:37,298
The demo deliberately reverts, so this is a reproducible failed receipt.

8
00:00:37,298 --> 00:00:42,404
The proof establishes the failure, not who was at fault.

9
00:00:42,704 --> 00:00:46,432
After attestation, the relayer obtains a proof.

10
00:00:46,432 --> 00:00:50,692
Creditcoin verifies it through the native Attestcoin precompile.

11
00:00:50,692 --> 00:00:58,148
The vault then reads those same verified bytes and checks every sponsor policy condition.

12
00:00:58,148 --> 00:01:01,343
Attestation preparation time is shown separately.

13
00:01:01,643 --> 00:01:07,737
The matching failed transaction receives the fixed sponsor rebate in test C T C.

14
00:01:07,737 --> 00:01:10,348
This is the mined claim receipt.

15
00:01:10,348 --> 00:01:16,442
A relayer may submit the proof, but cannot change the beneficiary or the amount.

16
00:01:16,742 --> 00:01:21,065
Repeating this claim is rejected by a read-only call.

17
00:01:21,065 --> 00:01:27,309
Local policy tests also reject an altered payload and a successful source receipt.

18
00:01:27,309 --> 00:01:31,152
These checks do not represent extra mined transactions.

19
00:01:31,452 --> 00:01:37,729
GasBack turns a remote failed receipt into a bounded, inspectable sponsorship decision.

20
00:01:37,729 --> 00:01:43,483
The source, proof, policy and payment evidence are available for review.

21
00:01:43,483 --> 00:01:46,622
All assets shown are test assets.
